 For decisions, `chat_template_kwargs` may be omitted, null, or an object containing only
 `enable_thinking: false`; other types, keys, or thinking values return HTTP 400.
 
+`TENSORFOLD_DECISION_IDS` gives decisions model ids of their own: `id=base` entries, commas or newlines apart, where
+`base` is `--name`, an `--alias` or a `TENSORFOLD_IDENTITIES` id. `GET /v1/models` lists each id; `/v1/decisions` and
+`/v1/systemone` score a request naming one through its base (an identity's rows for an identity's base), and a text
+route refuses it with HTTP 400. A request naming an identity id itself scores through that identity too.
+Flash Next on CUDA takes a score in steps between decode rounds: while other streams decode, a round's steps feed at
+most `TENSORFOLD_DECISION_ROWS` prompt rows between the running scores (256 by default), and steps take at most
+`TENSORFOLD_DECISION_SHARE` of the engine's time (0.1 by default), so the streams keep decoding; with nothing decoding
+a score runs whole. On a GB10, a stream decoding 75.7 tok/s alone decoded 72.4 beside back-to-back decisions on a
+1,806-token input, which took 4.3 s each meanwhile and 0.84 s on an idle server. A decision's own cache sits outside the streams' memory plan, so a prompt
+longer than `TENSORFOLD_DECISION_MAX_TOKENS` (16,384 by default) fails with HTTP 500.
+
